1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,319
This is a fictional student diary for the Kanqual demonstration.

2
00:00:04,669 --> 00:00:06,923
The voice is synthesized.

3
00:00:07,273 --> 00:00:10,162
I'm Eli, a third-year student.

4
00:00:10,512 --> 00:00:16,146
I commute about forty minutes, and I work at a grocery store four evenings a week.

5
00:00:16,496 --> 00:00:18,475
I like my classes.

6
00:00:18,825 --> 00:00:21,249
I want to be clear about that.

7
00:00:21,599 --> 00:00:26,893
My seminar professor knows my name, and our group project is going well.

8
00:00:27,243 --> 00:00:32,511
But being comfortable in a classroom isn't the same as feeling part of the university.

9
00:00:32,861 --> 00:00:35,985
I saw the Stories After Hours poster.

10
00:00:36,335 --> 00:00:39,594
Poetry and music, free entry.

11
00:00:39,944 --> 00:00:43,518
It sounded like exactly the kind of thing I'd enjoy.

12
00:00:43,868 --> 00:00:45,967
Then I looked at the time.

13
00:00:46,317 --> 00:00:48,431
Eight until ten at night.

14
00:00:48,781 --> 00:00:55,930
My last practical bus connection leaves before it's over, and on Fridays I'm usually closing at work anyway.

15
00:00:56,280 --> 00:00:58,834
Free doesn't mean I can get there.

16
00:00:59,184 --> 00:01:02,378
People say, you should get involved.

17
00:01:02,728 --> 00:01:05,597
They mean it kindly, mostly.

18
00:01:05,947 --> 00:01:10,450
But it starts to sound as though being left out is something I'm choosing.

19
00:01:10,800 --> 00:01:16,774
I can't keep explaining my shift schedule every time someone asks why I wasn't at an event.

20
00:01:17,124 --> 00:01:20,518
Yesterday I tried the Between Classes lunch.

21
00:01:20,868 --> 00:01:23,332
I only had twenty minutes.

22
00:01:23,682 --> 00:01:26,736
Nobody made it strange when I left early.

23
00:01:27,086 --> 00:01:33,099
Another commuter told me there's a group chat where people arrange study sessions before their buses.

24
00:01:33,449 --> 00:01:34,968
I joined it.

25
00:01:35,318 --> 00:01:38,227
So I don't want to say nothing works.

26
00:01:38,577 --> 00:01:43,131
That lunch worked because somebody had thought about when we'd actually be here.

27
00:01:43,481 --> 00:01:48,294
The university promotion makes campus look like one big shared living room.

28
00:01:48,644 --> 00:01:53,238
I watch that and wonder where the people who leave at three fit into the picture.

29
00:01:53,588 --> 00:01:56,427
I don't need to be in an advertisement.

30
00:01:56,777 --> 00:02:02,860
I need a place to sit without buying coffee, and plans that don't always start after dinner.

31
00:02:03,210 --> 00:02:06,869
There's a listening session called Make Room next month.

32
00:02:07,219 --> 00:02:11,823
I'll be working, but the flier says written comments are welcome.

33
00:02:12,173 --> 00:02:13,992
I might leave one.

34
00:02:14,342 --> 00:02:18,311
I want to know what happens after the comments, though.

35
00:02:18,661 --> 00:02:23,530
If they post a summary and change even one event time, I'll notice.

36
00:02:23,880 --> 00:02:30,068
Belonging would mean I don't have to rearrange my whole life just to have a small part in campus life.